<header><p class="enc-kicker">Religion / idea · religion</p><h1 class="enc-title">Nizari Isma'ilism</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Nizari, Nizar</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Nizari <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ismailism">Isma'ilism</a> is a branch of Ismaili <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/shiism">Shi'ism</a> that arose from the Fatimid succession crisis of 1094, when supporters of the designated heir Nizar rejected the accession of al-Musta'li. Under <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hasan-i-sabbah">Hasan-i Sabbah</a> it established a state based at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/alamut">Alamut</a> that opposed the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/seljuk-empire">Seljuk Empire</a>. The branch survives today under the leadership of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/aga-khan">Aga Khan</a>.</p></div>
